# Payroll, cash advances, payslips and HR Settings, built 2026-10-30. Expects outline_insert.ps1 loaded and the outline open.
Insert-After "Payslip shows days worked" @(
  "Built Oct 30, 2026: Compute makes a draft (can be done again); the HR Supervisor or an Admin finalizes it, which is refused while missing scans or overtime approvals are pending. Finalizing takes the cash advances and locks those attendance days. Payslips print one page each or save as one PDF; Payslip History keeps them.",
  "Rules approved by the owner (Oct 30, 2026): a Regular holiday not worked is paid, a Special holiday is not, and work on a holiday is paid as a normal day; leaving early is deducted like late minutes; government deductions use a monthly basis of daily rate x 26 days with the 2025 employee shares (SSS 5% of the salary credit, PhilHealth 2.5%, Pag-IBIG 2% up to 10,000), half per office payday and 12/52 per site payday, plus income tax from the TRAIN table. All rates are editable in Settings; the accountant should check them.",
  "HR Settings tab (Admin and HR Supervisor): work hours, grace minutes, work days, overtime rate and minimum, government rates, and holidays (Regular / Special).")
